# Who must approve a change to each part of the spec before it merges. GitHub asks them for a review on every
# pull request that touches their files. Turn on branch protection for main, with "Require review from Code Owners",
# so the pull request cannot merge without them.
# Replace the example teams with your own. The last matching line wins.

# Default: the product designer approves any change to the spec.
# /spec/                  @your-org/product-design

# The external rules: someone who can read the law, the regulator's guidance or the contract.
# /spec/sources/          @your-org/legal

# The product decisions and the open questions: product.
# /spec/decisions.md      @your-org/product
# /spec/decisions-replaced.md @your-org/product
# /spec/questions.md      @your-org/product

# The persona sheets: research.
# /spec/personas/         @your-org/research

# Each feature: its owner approves its flow, its screens and its feature decision log.
# /spec/flows/answer-a-request.md   @your-org/requests-team
# /spec/screens/request.md          @your-org/requests-team

# A proposed decision (Status: proposed) names in Decided by the person who must approve it. Make that person,
# or their team, the owner of the file it lives in, so the pull request waits for them.
